  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Arkansas federal contracts totaled $59.9M in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 95.5% year over year. The state recorded 312 awards with an average award size of $192K. FY2027 to date is a partial fiscal-year total. FY22 obligations were $1.4B, FY23 obligations were $1.6B, FY24 obligations were $2.1B, FY25 obligations were $1.4B, and FY26 obligations were $1.3B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer so far with $42.9M in obligations. BRISTON CONSTRUCTION, LLC is the largest vendor so far with $14.2M in obligations. Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction is the largest industry by obligations so far with $14.2M. The top ten buying agencies and vendors show a concentration of dollars: the top two buyers account for a large share of FY2027 to date obligations, and the top two vendors account for a large share of vendor obligations. All figures are contract obligations, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most in Arkansas right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs leads with $42.9M in FY2027 to date obligations. The Department of Justice follows with $8.7M, and the Department of the Interior follows with $3.4M. The Department of Energy and the Department of Agriculture round out the next largest buyers with $2.1M and $1.9M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top vendors and industries getting federal awards in Arkansas?",
        "body": "BRISTON CONSTRUCTION, LLC is the top vendor with $14.2M in FY2027 to date obligations. JETT'S SPECIALTY CONTRACTING, LLC and SHAVER FOODS LLC follow with $10.2M and $5.6M respectively. Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction are the top industries with $14.2M and $10.3M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
